/* Settings › Performance › Disable all animations. BakeryAppManager adds this style sheet to the app root, and takes
   it off again: nothing else changes. The ID selector (#app, the root's name) outranks every class-based rule in the
   game, so one rule is enough:
   - animation-name: none takes every UIAnimationClip off (the starbursts stop spinning, the mascot stops bobbing);
   - transition-duration: 0s makes every transition happen at once (page slides, dialogs, toasts);
   - --be-motion: none on the root stops the code-drawn art (falling particles, blinking, the wavy titles, the
     pills' count-up): it reads the property up its ancestors (ArtKit.MotionAllowed). */

#app {
    --be-motion: none;
}

#app * {
    animation-name: none;
    transition-duration: 0s;
}
